<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to July 9, as released by the Bank of Japan on Thursday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.44 (0.44)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.55 (0.57)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.98 (1.01)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.40 (0.40)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.50 (0.52)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.31 (0.31)	 three years  0.93 (0.97)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.35 (0.35)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.45 (0.48)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.26)	 three years  0.89 (0.92)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Jul 14 - Jul 18:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.58 (0.57)   120-150 days  0.68 (0.69)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.59 (0.60)   150-180 days  0.70 (0.72)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.60 (0.62)   180-360 days  0.72 (0.72)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.67 (0.68)   over 360 days 0.92 (0.90)</p>
</text>
